{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Break off.</b> Aharon intended for the sake of Heaven. He said: If I tell them, let a dog or Nachshon be head over you — if they appoint him over themselves, when Moshe comes and they depose him from his greatness, strife will multiply among them and they will come to bloodshed. And if I say: I will not give a head over them — they will appoint one themselves, and there will be strife. And if I say: I will be head over them — perhaps it will be hard in Moshe's eyes. I will keep them occupied with things that have no substance until Moshe comes. Therefore he said: break off — because the women are possessive of their jewelry, and it will create confusion in the matter."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:27.003410836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}